senses.gloss:
(I)--a hill tribe;
1: Br. II. १६. ६७; III. ४८. २३, ४४ and ४९; वा. ८८. १२२; ९८. १०७.
were defeated by परशुराम, Sagara and Bharata; punished with half shaving;
2: भा. IX. 8. 5; २०. ३०; III. ४१. ३९; Vi. IV. 3. ४२;
were denied the Vedic study and sacrifice and hence reduced to Mlecchahood.
3: Ib. IV. 3. ४८.

(II)--the १८ kings (ten-वा। प्।) of, ruled for ३८० years;
1: M. ५०. ७६; २७३. १८; वा. ९९. २६८, ३२४, ३५९, ३६१.
kingdom of;
2: M. ११४. ४१; १२१. ४५; १४४. ५७.
contemporaries of the शिशुनागस्, and after Gardabins; to be conquered by Kalki.
3: Br. III. ६३. १२०, १३४; ७३. १०८; ७४. १३७. १७२ and १७५; Vi. IV. 3. ४७.

--the science of birds, etc;
1: M. २१५. 9;
in connec- tion with founding temples.
2: Ib. २४०. १५; २६४. 9.

(I)--(शक्त्रि-ब्र्। प्।) the eldest of the १०० sons of वसिष्ठ and अरुन्धती. Father of पराशर through अदृ- श्यन्ति;
1: भा. IV. 1. ४१; Br. I. 1. 9; III. 8. ९१; ३६. 6; M. २०१. ३०; वा. 1. १७४; ७०. ८३.
a sage by tapas; a वेदव्यास. Heard the वायु पुराण from दक्ष and narrated it to पराशर in embryo;
2: Br. II. ३२; ९९ and ११५; ३५. १२४; IV. 4. ६५; M. १९६. २६; वा. १०३. ६५.
a resident of ब्रह्मक्षेत्र;
3: वा. ५९. ९१, १०५.
cursed king कल्माषपाद in नैमिष.
4: Ib. 2. १०-11.

(X)--of विष्णु; is प्रधान purus2a1tmaka; this energy separates at the deluge and unites at the time of creation;
1: Vi. II. 7. ३१-2.
something like fire in wood or oil in sesamum; from प्रधान germinate intellect and rudiments of things and from them Asuras;
2: Ib. II. 7. ३३-9.
प्रधान compared to a tree; विष्णु is मूल-prakr2ti or the primary nature in whom all beings [page३-359+ २७] exist and all finally immerse;
3: Ib. II. 7. ४२-3.
is three-fold made up of the three energies of Hari.
4: Ib. VI. 8. 7.

(V)--Indra;
1: Vi. V. ११. 1; २९. 1; ३०. 4 and २६; ३४. 1.
attended on Diti and cut the embryo in seven parts and later into forty-nine pieces; these are the Maruts;
2: Ib. I. २१. ३३, ४०.
city of वशन्कसार;
3: Ib. II. 8. 9.
joined बृहस्पति in the तार- कामय;
4: Ib. IV. 6. १६.
father of Arjuna.
5: Ib. IV. २०. ४०.

--thirty-two lakhs of योजनस् in extent and encircled by sea of curds (दधिमण्डोद) (क्षीरोद-वि। प्।) of equal dimension; takes its name from a great शाक tree; ruled by a son of Priyavrata, मेधातिथि who divided it among his seven sons and retired to forest; here वायु is wor- shipped by प्राणायाम;
1: भा. V. २०. २४-28.
divided into seven kingdoms bear- ing the respective names of the seven sons of the first king Havya (Bhavya-वि। प्।), a grandson of स्वायम्भुव; con- tains seven streams, several towns and villages; people here follow svadharma and वर्णाश्रम dharma;
2: Br. II. १४. १३; १९. २७, ८०-107; २१. ७३; वा. ३३. १३; ४९. ७४; ५०. १२७.
seven moun- tains;
3: M. १२२. 1.
one of the seven continents, double the size of the क्रौञ्चद्वीप; the four castes in it; Vangas, Magadhas, मानसस् and Mandagas; विष्णु stands in the form of सूर्य.
4: Vi. II. 1. १४; 2. 5; IV. ५८. ७१.
